Subject: [PATCH] Windows: VSync for GL's own swap (TODO 420)

Where the DXGI swap chain is not used (Intel's drivers, where GL cannot draw into Direct3D's textures), GL's own swap
shows the window's pictures, and on Windows the VSync setting never reached it: the swap kept WGL's default interval
of 1, VSync on whatever the setting. A level whose frames took a little more than a refresh was shown at every second
(or third) refresh: exactly 30 (ThinkPad, UHD 620) or 20 (Vostro, Iris Xe) pictures a second at a cap of 60, with the
frame-rate cap and the VSync setting changing nothing. The setting is now the swap interval there as on Linux: Off 0,
else 1 (raylib's window flag, set and then cleared for Off: ClearWindowState changes the interval only for a flag it
holds). PS2X_GL_SWAP_SYNC=0: the interval left as before.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present.cpp
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present.cpp
@@ -166,6 +166,25 @@
                 else
                     ClearWindowState(FLAG_VSYNC_HINT);
             }
+#else
+            // (TODO 420) Windows: GL's swap is the present where the DXGI swap chain is not used (Intel's drivers: GL cannot
+            // draw into Direct3D's textures there) - the VSync setting as its swap interval too: Off 0, else 1. Never set
+            // before, the swap kept WGL's default interval of 1: VSync on whatever the setting, so a frame a little over a
+            // refresh waited for the next one - a level at exactly 30 (ThinkPad, UHD 620) or 20 (Vostro, Iris Xe) pictures a
+            // second at a cap of 60 where the GPU's work was 11-25 ms a frame. raylib changes the interval only for a flag
+            // it holds (SetWindowState sets 1, ClearWindowState sets 0 only when the flag is set): both, for Off.
+            // PS2X_GL_SWAP_SYNC=0: the interval left as it was (WGL's 1).
+            static const bool glSwapSync = !(std::getenv("PS2X_GL_SWAP_SYNC") && *std::getenv("PS2X_GL_SWAP_SYNC") == '0');
+            static int applied = -1;
+            const int wanted = sync() == 0 ? 0 : 1;
+            if (glSwapSync && wanted != applied)
+            {
+                applied = wanted;
+                SetWindowState(FLAG_VSYNC_HINT);
+                if (!wanted)
+                    ClearWindowState(FLAG_VSYNC_HINT);
+                std::fprintf(stderr, "[present] GL's own swap: VSync %s (swap interval %d)\n", wanted ? "on" : "off", wanted);
+            }
 #endif
             EndDrawing();
             return;
